-- 1. the matchmaker module
local MM_SRC = [=====[-- ServerScripts/[Server] Init/GameManager/Managers/MatchmakingManager (ModuleScript)
-- ONLINE matchmaking: the queues behind the PLAY button. Every lobby server shares them
-- (MemoryStoreService), so you're matched with whoever is searching anywhere, not just here.
-- (The pads in the Deployment wing are the LOBBY queues: only people in this server. See QueueManager.)
--
-- Queues (LobbyConfig.Queues): 1v1, 2v2 and 3v3, each casual and ranked. Every queue is separate.
-- Ranked needs account level LobbyConfig.RankedLevel (in Studio, LobbyConfig.StudioUnlockRanked opens it).
--
-- How a match is made
--   * Searching puts { user, server, rating, time } into the queue's sorted map (oldest first). This
--     server keeps the entry alive while you wait; if the server dies, the entry expires by itself.
--   * Each queue has a short lease (MM_Locks). Only the server holding it runs the matchmaker for
--     that queue, so two servers can never build two matches out of the same players.
--   * The matchmaker takes the longest-waiting players (ranked: inside a rating gap that widens the
--     longer you wait), claims them atomically, reserves a match server and writes the match into
--     MM_Results for each player.
--   * Every server checks MM_Results for its own searching players and teleports them into that
--     reserved server with TeleportData = { Mode, Ranked, Queue, MatchId, Teams, Loadouts, From, Online }.
-- What the UI reads: player attributes MM_Queue (queue id), MM_Status (Searching | Found | Teleporting),
-- MM_Since (server time you started), and ReplicatedStorage attribute MM_Counts (JSON: queue id -> searching).
-- Stepping onto a lobby pad while searching online takes you out of the online queue.

local Players = game:GetService("Players")
local ReplicatedStorage = game:GetService("ReplicatedStorage")
local ServerScriptService = game:GetService("ServerScriptService")
local RunService = game:GetService("RunService")
local TeleportService = game:GetService("TeleportService")
